==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|riff-raff}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fro|rif}} {{m|fro|et|}} {{m|fro|raf||one and all}}, of {{der|en|gem|-}} origin.  The first word is from {{m|fro|rifler||to scrape off}} and the last is from {{m|fro|raffler}}, related to {{m|fro|rafler||to plunder}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɪfɹæf/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-riffraff.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# The [[rabble]]; [[crowds]]; the common people.
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:commonalty}}
#: {{ux|en|They started charging a modest fee in an effort to keep the '''riffraff''' out.}}
